    "body": "## Summary\n\nCloses ADR-029 by flipping status to Implemented, adding an Implementation section, and updating CHANGELOG. **Documentation only — no code changes.**\n\n## The Implementation section records the two-stage measurement\n\n`.mw-page-container-inner` y-coordinate on Wikipedia at viewport 1774:\n\n| Stage | y-coordinate | Delta vs baseline |\n|---|---|---|\n| Baseline (pre-ADR-029) | 585 | — |\n| Commit 2 alone (flex, no flip) | 750 | **+165 (regression)** |\n| **Commit 2 + Commit 3** (flex + flip) | **59** | **−526 (payoff)** |\n\nHeader height, same viewports:\n\n| Element | Commit 2 | Commit 2+3 |\n|---|---|---|\n| `.vector-header-container` | 727 | **36** |\n| `.vector-header-start` | 711 | **5** |\n| `.vector-header-end` | 20 | 20 |\n\nArticle content above the fold for the first time in the CSS-layout arc.\n\n## Honest about the unplanned Commit 3\n\nThe original ADR-029 spec planned **three commits**: parser, algorithm, docs. Actual scope was **three PRs** with **Commit 3 (feature-class flip) unplanned** — added after Commit 2's verification revealed a +165px regression.\n\n**This is the first time the measure-predict-verify-correct pattern caught a regression before merge** rather than correcting the record after (cf. ADR-028's post-hoc misdiagnosis correction). Same discipline, applied preventively.\n\nRoot cause of the regression: Wikipedia ships `<html class=\"... vector-feature-main-menu-pinned-disabled ...\">` when fetched without JS. An inline `<script>` flips that to `-enabled` at desktop viewports. Without the flip, `.vector-main-menu-landmark` stays visible at 711px (mobile hamburger menu stacked as blocks), pushing the grid container down by 165px. Commit 3 mimics the JS flip in `RenderPipeline::relayout()` — ~15 lines, before the cascade, idempotent across resizes.\n\n## Also documented: four small bugs fixed in Commit 2\n\n1. **`ComputedStyle::get` signature** — takes `const std::string&`, not `std::string_view`. `get_prop` lambda adjusted.\n2. **Explicit `flex-basis: 0` was treated as natural size** — breaks `flex: 1 1 0` semantics (both children fall back to content sizes; grow gets no free space to distribute). Removed the \"parsed > 0\" guard.\n3. **Flex test harness didn't zero UA default `body { margin: 8px }`** — `x=0` assertions were off by 8px. Prepended `body,html{margin:0;padding:0}` in `flex_prep`.\n4. **(Test-only) Initial `align-items` test used inline `style=\"height:...\"`** — the test cascade doesn't parse inline styles, so children were natural-height and the cross-axis offset was 0. Rewritten to use nested divs at natural heights (`fake_measure` yields 16px per line).\n\n## What changed\n\n- `docs/decisions/029-flex-layout.md` — Status: Accepted → **Implemented**; new **Implementation** section at line 387 (85 lines) before Verification\n- `CHANGELOG.md` — two new `### Added` entries: **Flex layout** and **Viewport feature-class flip**\n\n## What didn't change\n\n- Zero code changes\n- Test count unchanged: 392 cases / 1637 assertions\n- Full suite green\n- No behavior change to main\n\n## Deferred (unchanged from ADR-029's spec)\n\n- `flex-wrap: wrap` (multi-line flex)\n- `row-reverse`, `column-reverse`\n- `align-self`, `align-content`\n- `order`\n- `inline-flex` as inline-level\n- Percentage cross-axis `flex-basis`\n\n## The arc closes\n\nADR-029 completes the CSS-layout arc from ADR-018 through ADR-029:\n\n- 14 ADRs delivered (018–029)\n- 24 PRs merged (#137–#163)\n- 392 tests / 1637 assertions\n- Zero regressions\n- Wikipedia now renders article content **above the fold** for the first time\n\nRefs #161 #162 #163\n",
